=== SURVEY ===
Mapped the web `components/charts` surface (prompt's explicit list). Reused TSChartPalette/tokens + the
P3-0001 components (TSCard/TSButton/TSRangeSlider/TSClipboard). Swift Charts (`import Charts`) provides
LineMark/AreaMark/BarMark/PointMark/SectorMark/RuleMark; radar has no native mark (drawn with Canvas).

=== REASONING ===
- Shared data model: TSChartPoint / TSChartSeries / TSChartSlice (palette-colored), so every chart consumes
  one typed shape. Pure helpers (TSChartFormat.axisLabel/downsample/toggleHidden/summary, TSChartGradient)
  are unit-tested.
- Safe formatting: axisLabel renders "—" for non-finite (never "nan"); large series downsample to <=300/maxCount.
- Accessibility (ADR-015): every chart carries an accessibilityLabel; radar/gauge expose an accessibilityValue
  summary; TSChartContainer surfaces a concise summary line; legend toggles carry .isSelected.
- Empty/error: TSChartContainer renders a self-contained empty overlay (feedback components are a later prompt,
  P3-0004) and never hides the panel.
- Interaction: time markers + annotation lines are @ChartContentBuilder helpers (embedded in a Chart{});
  TSChartBrush reuses the accessible TSRangeSlider for the x-window (vs a fragile custom gesture);
  add/list annotation surfaces are binding/action wrappers.
- Performance: animations honor Reduce Motion via TSAnimation (from P2); downsampling caps mark counts.

=== CHANGES === (apps/apple/Sources/Components/Charts/** — 8 files, ~22 components/utilities)
  + ChartModels.swift     TSChartPoint, TSChartSeries, TSChartSlice, TSChartFormat (pure), TSChartGradient
  + ChartContainer.swift  TSChartContainer (title/export/empty/summary), TSChartLegend (toggle)
